+  /*!
+    \brief Batched directed bounds: down-rounded and up-rounded image in ONE
+    nearest-rounding region.
+
+    Each <f>_dn_up evaluates the correctly-rounded routine at x_dn (rounded
+    down into *lo) and x_up (rounded up into *hi) inside a single
+    round_nearest()/round_upward() pair instead of two -- the two mathlib calls
+    share the nearest window, halving the FPU mode toggles per interval
+    transcendental. BIT-IDENTICAL to calling <f>_dn(x_dn) then <f>_up(x_up):
+    same routine, same rounding mode, same outward ulp bump; only the
+    placement/count of the mode switches changes.
+    \caution Valid only from an FE_UPWARD ambient (restored on exit). The
+    caller's argument reduction must stay in FE_UPWARD and never enter this
+    nearest window.
